  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a string `word`.\n\nOutput the **largest** number of non-intersecting **substrings** of word that are at **least** four characters long and start and end with the same letter.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** word = \"abcdeafdef\"\n\n**Output:** 2\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe two substrings are `\"abcdea\"` and `\"fdef\"`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** word = \"bcdaaaab\"\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe only substring is `\"aaaa\"`. Keep in mind that we cannot **also** choose `\"bcdaaaab\"` since it intersects with the other substring.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= word.length <= 2 * 105`\n* `word` consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
